{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/e2e/_toolchain.py::provision_toolchain` evaluates `_satisfied()` BEFORE taking the\n`flock`, and `_satisfied` treats the harness bundle as ready on mere existence\n(`(js_dir / BUNDLE_RELPATH).is_file()`). esbuild writes `dist/roundtrip.mjs` in place, so\nunder `-n 4 --dist worksteal` a worker can observe the path exist while the lock holder is\nstill writing it, return early from the unlocked fast path, and run\n`node dist/roundtrip.mjs` against a truncated file. The failure surfaces as a confusing\nharness/JSON error rather than as a provisioning problem.\n\nRaised as an LLM-Review advisory on change 2600 (`tests/e2e/_toolchain.py:151`). NOT a\nregression from 2600: before it there was no lock at all and workers raced freely; 2600\nnarrowed the window and this closes the remainder. History and the duplicate-merge notes are\nin the comments.\n\n## Approach\n\nDelete the unlocked fast path; evaluate `_satisfied()` INSIDE `_install_lock`. The `npm`\nlookup moves inside the lock too, after the readiness check, so an already-provisioned tree\non a host without `npm` still returns cleanly rather than newly raising. This is a MOVEMENT\nof an existing check, not new machinery: no new lock, env var, config key, feature flag, CI\ngate, fixture or helper, so the mechanism-delta ratchet must stay at zero.\n\nAn `fcntl.flock` on a local file costs microseconds and is taken a handful of times per run\n(once per xdist worker at collection, plus at most once per session in the fixture\nfallback), so the fast path buys almost nothing while creating the window. A waiter blocks\nonly while a peer is genuinely provisioning, and it waits during COLLECTION, which is off\nevery test's timeout budget - the property bug 9a17-e0b3-7aa6-4091 established.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/e2e/_toolchain.py` - move the `_satisfied()` and `npm`-lookup checks inside\n  `_install_lock`; drop the pre-lock fast path.\n- `tests/e2e/test_toolchain_provisioning.py` - add a deterministic forced-interleaving\n  reproduction, and extend the existing two-process concurrency oracle to bracket the build\n  step as well as the install.\n\n## Reproduction strategy\n\nThe reproduction FORCES the interleaving; it does not spawn N workers and hope. A child\nprocess takes the provisioning `flock`, and while HOLDING it creates exactly the state the\nfast path inspects - `node_modules/`, `node_modules/playwright/`, and a half-written\n`dist/roundtrip.mjs` - appends `peer-mid-build` to an append-only log, sleeps, appends\n`peer-done`, and only then releases. The test waits for `peer-mid-build` to appear (so the\nhalf-written state provably exists first), calls `provision_toolchain`, and appends\n`caller-returned`. The log order is the oracle:\n\n- pre-fix the unlocked fast path fires immediately and the log reads\n  `peer-mid-build, caller-returned, peer-done`;\n- post-fix the caller blocks on the lock and it reads\n  `peer-mid-build, peer-done, caller-returned`.\n\nNo sleep-and-hope, no repetition: the interleaving is constructed, so the RED is reproducible\non demand in real time.\n\nThe existing two-process test brackets only the install step; its stub is extended to bracket\n`run build` as well, and it asserts every span in the merged log closes before the next one\nopens, across both processes and both steps.\n\nUncontended behaviour is confirmed unchanged by the rest of the module, which already pins\nthe no-op-when-satisfied case, the missing-`npm` case, the unusable-lock case, the\nwithout-then-with-browser completion case, and a real nested pytest collection that asserts\nexactly one install per selection.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `provision_toolchain` performs NO readiness check outside the lock: reading\n      `tests/e2e/_toolchain.py` shows the `_satisfied()` call only inside the\n      `with _install_lock(js_dir):` block, and no `return` precedes it.\n- [x] A caller never returns while a peer is mid-build, proven DETERMINISTICALLY by the\n      forced-interleaving test described above (constructed lock-held half-written state, not\n      repetition).\n- [x] DEFECT-SEEDED PROOF: restoring the unlocked fast path makes that test FAIL again. The\n      mutation output is quoted in the ticket trail and the mutation reverted - a race test\n      that passes because the race did not fire is otherwise indistinguishable from one that\n      passes because the race is fixed.\n- [x] An already-satisfied tree on a host with no `npm` still returns cleanly (no new\n      `npm not on PATH` failure introduced by moving the lookup under the lock).\n- [x] No regression in the uncontended path: the whole existing provisioning module passes,\n      and a cold single-worker run provisions exactly once.\n- [x] No new mechanism is registered, and no `# mechanism-ok:` marker is added.\n\n## Testing\n\nEach criterion names the command that proves it, run from the worktree venv\n(`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" ...`):\n\n- AC1 (no unlocked check): `git diff` on `tests/e2e/_toolchain.py`, plus\n  `python -m pytest tests/e2e/test_toolchain_provisioning.py -q`.\n- AC2 (deterministic reproduction):\n  `python -m pytest tests/e2e/test_toolchain_provisioning.py -q -k half_written` - GREEN\n  after the fix.\n- AC3 (defect-seeded proof): re-insert the pre-lock\n  `if _satisfied(js_dir, with_browser=with_browser): return`, re-run the AC2 command and\n  observe RED with the interleaved log in the assertion message, then `git checkout` the\n  mutation away and re-run to GREEN.\n- AC4 (satisfied tree without npm):\n  `python -m pytest tests/e2e/test_toolchain_provisioning.py -q -k \"satisfied or missing_npm\"`.\n- AC5 (no regression): `python -m pytest tests/e2e/test_toolchain_provisioning.py -q` in full,\n  and a cold `python -m pytest tests/e2e -q -p no:randomly --collect-only` over a cleaned\n  `tests/e2e/js` showing one install and one build.\n- AC6 (ratchets): `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` AND\n  `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py -q` - BOTH, because `make lint` runs\n  only the first and that gap has already sent a sibling change to Gerrit red.\n- Whole-tree gates: `make lint` and `make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788522213755667001,"uuid":"0173d2f2-71eb-4373-ac40-6bb1d9a69fb6"}